data.content:
Created both files. Here's a summary:

**`SortableList.razor`** — Generic (`@typeparam TItem`) markup with a `<ul>` loop. Each `<li>` renders the `ItemTemplate` plus Move Up/Down buttons, disabled at the boundaries. Uses `@key` for efficient diffing.

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — `partial class` code-behind:
- **Copies** `Items` into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the parent's list).
- `MoveUp`/`MoveDown` swap adjacent items, then invoke `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only snapshot.

Usage matches your example — just note the callback receives `IReadOnlyList<TItem>`:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = new() { /* ... */ };

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
